/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Deuteronomy chapters 11-15
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("deuteronomy", [
{n:11, name:"Blessing and Curse", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 11:26",verse:"Behold, I set before you this day a blessing and a curse;"}, facts:["Did you know Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal still face each other across the valley of Shechem, the blessing on one and the curse on the other, exactly where Moses pointed (Deuteronomy 11:29)?","Did you know the 'first rain and the latter rain' follow the real farming calendar of Canaan: early rains in autumn to soften the ground for sowing, latter rains in spring to ripen the harvest (Deuteronomy 11:14)?","Did you know the promised land is called 'a land which the LORD thy God careth for,' with His eyes always upon it, unlike Egypt which was watered by foot like a garden (Deuteronomy 11:10, 12)?"], questions:[
{q:"Whom does Moses say he is speaking to in this chapter?", options:["Those who have seen God's chastisement, His greatness, His mighty hand, and His stretched out arm","Their children, who had not yet known these things","The priests of the tabernacle alone","The kings of the nations round about"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:2",verse:"And know ye this day: for I speak not with your children which have not known, and which have not seen the chastisement of the LORD your God, his greatness, his mighty hand, and his stretched out arm,", insight:"Moses speaks to eyewitnesses, not to legend keepers; faith rests on what God has done in plain sight."},
{q:"What did God do to the horses and chariots of Egypt?", options:["He made the waters of the Red Sea overflow them, and destroyed them","He turned them into pillars of stone","He scattered them in the wilderness","He gave them into Israel's hands"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:4",verse:"And what he did unto the army of Egypt, unto their horses, and to their chariots; how he made the water of the Red sea to overflow them as they pursued after you, and how the LORD hath destroyed them unto this day;", insight:"The sea that closed over Egypt's army still preaches: no power outruns the God who parts waters."},
{q:"What happened to Dathan and Abiram?", options:["The earth opened her mouth and swallowed them, and their households","They were driven out of the camp","They were made priests instead","They fled back into Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:6",verse:"And what he did unto Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, the son of Reuben: how the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them up, and their households, and their tents, and all the substance that was in their possession, in the midst of all Israel:", insight:"The earth itself opened against rebellion; some sins the ground will not hold."},
{q:"What does Moses say his hearers' eyes have seen?", options:["All the great acts of the LORD","The lands beyond the river","The idols of the nations","The armies of the kings"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:7",verse:"But your eyes have seen all the great acts of the LORD which he did.", insight:"Their eyes had seen; memory was meant to become obedience."},
{q:"Why does Moses tell Israel to keep all the commandments?", options:["That they may be strong, and go in and possess the land","That Egypt may fear them","That the priests may rule over them","That their enemies may pay them tribute"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:8",verse:"Therefore shall ye keep all the commandments which I command you this day, that ye may be strong, and go in and possess the land, whither ye go to possess it;", insight:"Strength for the journey flows through obedience; keep the word and you keep the land."},
{q:"How did the land of Egypt get its water?", options:["It was watered with the foot, as a garden of herbs","It drank only from the rain of heaven","It was watered from the Jordan","It needed no water at all"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:10",verse:"For the land, whither thou goest in to possess it, is not as the land of Egypt, from whence ye came out, where thou sowedst thy seed, and wateredst it with thy foot, as a garden of herbs:", insight:"Egypt's gardens ran on human effort; the promised land would run on heaven's mercy."},
{q:"What is the promised land like?", options:["A land of hills and valleys, drinking water of the rain of heaven","A flat plain watered by canals","A desert of hidden wells","A land of ice and snow"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:11",verse:"But the land, whither ye go to possess it, is a land of hills and valleys, and drinketh water of the rain of heaven:", insight:"Hills and valleys that drink from heaven; God designed dependence into the very soil."},
{q:"What does the LORD do for the land?", options:["He careth for it, and His eyes are always upon it, from the year's beginning to the year's end","He visits it once a year","He leaves it to the nations","He forgets it in the winter"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:12",verse:"A land which the LORD thy God careth for: the eyes of the LORD thy God are always upon it, from the beginning of the year even unto the end of the year.", insight:"'The eyes of the LORD are always upon it'; the land, and His people, live under a constant gaze of care."},
{q:"What will God send if Israel hearkens diligently?", options:["The rain of the land in his due season, the first rain and the latter rain","Snow in the summer","Hail every month","Wells that never fail"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:14",verse:"That I will give you the rain of your land in his due season, the first rain and the latter rain, that thou mayest gather in thy corn, and thy wine, and thine oil.", insight:"First rain and latter rain in season; obedience opens the heavens on schedule."},
{q:"What warning does Moses give about the heart?", options:["Take heed, lest your heart be deceived, and ye turn aside and serve other gods","Guard your heart from all sadness","Keep your heart from the stranger","Hide your heart from the priest"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:16",verse:"Take heed to yourselves, that your heart be not deceived, and ye turn aside, and serve other gods, and worship them;", insight:"Deception starts in the heart before it reaches the altar; take heed is the first command."},
{q:"What happens if Israel serves other gods?", options:["The heaven is shut up, there is no rain, and the land yields not her fruit","The sun goes dark at noon","The rivers run backward","The mountains fall into the sea"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:17",verse:"And then the LORD’S wrath be kindled against you, and he shut up the heaven, that there be no rain, and that the land yield not her fruit; and lest ye perish quickly from off the good land which the LORD giveth you.", insight:"Idolatry shuts the heaven; false gods can never make it rain."},
{q:"What are Israel to do with God's words?", options:["Lay them up in heart and soul, bind them for a sign upon the hand, and as frontlets between the eyes","Write them only on the temple walls","Speak them once a year","Hide them from their children"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:18",verse:"Therefore shall ye lay up these my words in your heart and in your soul, and bind them for a sign upon your hand, that they may be as frontlets between your eyes.", insight:"Heart, hand, and head; God's word belongs inside you, on what you do, and before your eyes."},
{q:"When are parents to teach these words to their children?", options:["When sitting in the house, walking by the way, lying down, and rising up","Only on the feast days","Only in the tabernacle","Only when the children ask"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:19",verse:"And ye shall teach them your children, speaking of them when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way, when thou liest down, and when thou risest up.", insight:"Sitting, walking, lying, rising; teaching happens in the rhythm of ordinary days."},
{q:"Where are the words to be written?", options:["Upon the door posts of the house, and upon the gates","Upon their garments","Upon their chariots","Upon altars of stone"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:20",verse:"And thou shalt write them upon the door posts of thine house, and upon thy gates:", insight:"Door posts and gates; faith should greet everyone who enters and leaves your home."},
{q:"How long shall their days be multiplied?", options:["As the days of heaven upon the earth","As the days of the grass of the field","As the days of the moon","As the days of the flood"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:21",verse:"That your days may be multiplied, and the days of your children, in the land which the LORD sware unto your fathers to give them, as the days of heaven upon the earth.", insight:"Days like heaven on earth; obedience stretches life toward eternity's horizon."},
{q:"What threefold devotion does Moses require?", options:["Love the LORD, walk in all His ways, and cleave unto Him","Pray, fast, and give alms","Sing, dance, and shout","Build, plant, and harvest"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:22",verse:"For if ye shall diligently keep all these commandments which I command you, to do them, to love the LORD your God, to walk in all his ways, and to cleave unto him;", insight:"Love Him, walk with Him, cleave to Him; devotion is affection, direction, and attachment."},
{q:"What will God do to the nations greater and mightier than Israel?", options:["He will drive them out from before Israel","He will make them serve Israel","He will send them back to Egypt","He will hide them in the hills"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:23",verse:"Then will the LORD drive out all these nations from before you, and ye shall possess greater nations and mightier than yourselves.", insight:"Greater and mightier is no match for the God who drives them out; size means nothing to Him."},
{q:"How far would Israel's possession reach?", options:["Every place the soles of their feet tread, from the wilderness and Lebanon, from the river Euphrates to the uttermost sea","Only the valley of the Jordan","Only the land of Goshen","Only the hills of Ephraim"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:24",verse:"Every place whereon the soles of your feet shall tread shall be yours: from the wilderness and Lebanon, from the river, the river Euphrates, even unto the uttermost sea shall your coast be.", insight:"Every place the foot treads; possession follows the steps of faith."},
{q:"What does God promise about Israel's enemies?", options:["No man shall be able to stand before them, and the LORD will lay their fear upon all the land","Every enemy will love them","No enemy will ever be seen","Their enemies will rule over them"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:25",verse:"There shall no man be able to stand before you: for the LORD your God shall lay the fear of you and the dread of you upon all the land that ye shall tread upon, as he hath said unto you.", insight:"No man able to stand before you; God turns His people's fear into the enemy's terror."},
{q:"What does Moses set before Israel this day?", options:["A blessing, if ye obey, and a curse, if ye will not obey","Gold and silver from the nations","Two kings to choose between","War and peace"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 11:26",verse:"Behold, I set before you this day a blessing and a curse;", insight:"A blessing and a curse; every day lays the same two paths before us, and the choice is never neutral."}
]},
{n:12, name:"One Place of Worship", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 12:5",verse:"But unto the place which the LORD your God shall choose out of all your tribes to put his name there, even unto his habitation shall ye seek, and thither thou shalt come:"}, facts:["Did you know 'thou shalt not add thereto, nor diminish from it' closes the chapter like a seal on God's law, the same warning repeated near the end of Revelation (Deuteronomy 12:32)?","Did you know the command to destroy idolatrous places names their settings exactly: upon the high mountains, upon the hills, and under every green tree (Deuteronomy 12:2)?","Did you know 'the blood is the life' is the reason behind the no-blood rule: blood belongs on God's altar, not in man's stomach (Deuteronomy 12:23)?"], questions:[
{q:"What are Israel to do with the places where the nations served their gods?", options:["Utterly destroy them, upon the high mountains, upon the hills, and under every green tree","Build new altars there","Worship there themselves","Leave them alone for the priests"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:2",verse:"Ye shall utterly destroy all the places, wherein the nations which ye shall possess served their gods, upon the high mountains, and upon the hills, and under every green tree:", insight:"High mountains, hills, green trees; idolatry must be destroyed at its addresses, not at its excuses."},
{q:"What four things are Israel to do to the idolatrous shrines?", options:["Overthrow their altars, break their pillars, burn their groves with fire, and hew down their graven images","Wash them, paint them, repair them, and keep them","Move them into the tabernacle","Sell them to the nations"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:3",verse:"And ye shall overthrow their altars, and break their pillars, and burn their groves with fire; and ye shall hew down the graven images of their gods, and destroy the names of them out of that place.", insight:"Overthrow, break, burn, hew down; half measures leave idols standing."},
{q:"What does Moses say Israel shall not do unto the LORD?", options:["They shall not worship Him the way the nations worship their gods","They shall not sing unto Him","They shall not pray unto Him","They shall not come near unto Him"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:4",verse:"Ye shall not do so unto the LORD your God.", insight:"'Ye shall not do so unto the LORD your God'; true worship is not borrowed from idols."},
{q:"Where are Israel to seek the LORD?", options:["Unto the place which the LORD shall choose out of all their tribes to put His name there","Wherever it pleases them","In the high places","Under every green tree"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:5",verse:"But unto the place which the LORD your God shall choose out of all your tribes to put his name there, even unto his habitation shall ye seek, and thither thou shalt come:", insight:"One chosen place for His name; God, not man, chooses where He is worshipped."},
{q:"What are they to bring to that place?", options:["Burnt offerings, sacrifices, tithes, heave offerings, vows, freewill offerings, and firstlings","Only their silent prayers","Gifts for the poor alone","Swords and shields for war"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:6",verse:"And thither ye shall bring your burnt offerings, and your sacrifices, and your tithes, and heave offerings of your hand, and your vows, and your freewill offerings, and the firstlings of your herds and of your flocks:", insight:"Seven kinds of offerings; worship with empty hands is worship half done."},
{q:"What shall they do before the LORD at that place?", options:["Eat there before Him, and rejoice in all that they put their hand unto, with their households","Fast in silence","Sleep before the altar","Mourn for their sins"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:7",verse:"And there ye shall eat before the LORD your God, and ye shall rejoice in all that ye put your hand unto, ye and your households, wherein the LORD thy God hath blessed thee.", insight:"Eat and rejoice before Him; worship ends in feasting, not in gloom."},
{q:"What does Moses forbid them to do?", options:["Do every man whatsoever is right in his own eyes","Eat meat at home","Sing songs of praise","Keep the sabbath day"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:8",verse:"Ye shall not do after all the things that we do here this day, every man whatsoever is right in his own eyes.", insight:"'Right in his own eyes' is the oldest false worship; sincerity is no substitute for obedience."},
{q:"Why were they not to do these things yet?", options:["For they were not as yet come to the rest and to the inheritance","For the tabernacle was broken down","For the priests were too few","For the land was too small"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:9",verse:"For ye are not as yet come to the rest and to the inheritance, which the LORD your God giveth you.", insight:"Not yet come to the rest; some freedoms belong only on the other side of the Jordan."},
{q:"Who is to rejoice before the LORD?", options:["They and their sons, daughters, menservants, maidservants, and the Levite","Only the priests","Only the elders","Only the firstborn sons"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:12",verse:"And ye shall rejoice before the LORD your God, ye, and your sons, and your daughters, and your menservants, and your maidservants, and the Levite that is within your gates; forasmuch as he hath no part nor inheritance with you.", insight:"Sons, daughters, servants, the Levite; no one in the household is left out of the joy."},
{q:"What does Moses allow in all their gates?", options:["They may kill and eat flesh, whatsoever their soul lusteth after","They may offer sacrifices there","They may build altars there","They may worship as they please"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:15",verse:"Notwithstanding thou mayest kill and eat flesh in all thy gates, whatsoever thy soul lusteth after, according to the blessing of the LORD thy God which he hath given thee: the unclean and the clean may eat thereof, as of the roebuck, and as of the hart.", insight:"Flesh in all thy gates; God gives daily bread room, and keeps worship in His place."},
{q:"What are they never to eat?", options:["The blood; they shall pour it upon the earth as water","The fat of the ox","The marrow of the bones","The flesh of the lamb"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:16",verse:"Only ye shall not eat the blood; ye shall pour it upon the earth as water.", insight:"Blood poured as water; life belongs to God, and we return it to the earth."},
{q:"Whom must they not forsake?", options:["The Levite, as long as they live upon the earth","The stranger at the gate","The king in his palace","The merchant in the market"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:19",verse:"Take heed to thyself that thou forsake not the Levite as long as thou livest upon the earth.", insight:"Forsake not the Levite; the servant of God should never be the forgotten of men."},
{q:"What will happen when the LORD enlarges their border?", options:["They may eat flesh when their soul longeth to eat flesh","They must offer more sacrifices","They must build new cities","They must keep more feasts"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:20",verse:"When the LORD thy God shall enlarge thy border, as he hath promised thee, and thou shalt say, I will eat flesh, because thy soul longeth to eat flesh; thou mayest eat flesh, whatsoever thy soul lusteth after.", insight:"Enlarged borders, enlarged appetite; blessing widens the table, and the rules still stand."},
{q:"Why must they not eat the blood?", options:["Because the blood is the life, and they may not eat the life with the flesh","Because the blood is bitter","Because the blood is unclean to touch","Because the priests forbid it"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:23",verse:"Only be sure that thou eat not the blood: for the blood is the life; and thou mayest not eat the life with the flesh.", insight:"'The blood is the life'; take the meal, but leave the life to God."},
{q:"What are they to do with the blood?", options:["Pour it upon the earth as water","Drink it before the altar","Keep it in a vessel","Burn it in the fire"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:24",verse:"Thou shalt not eat it; thou shalt pour it upon the earth as water.", insight:"Poured as water upon the earth; the simplest acts can carry the deepest reverence."},
{q:"What will happen if they observe and hear all these words?", options:["It shall go well with them and their children after them for ever","They shall become rich","They shall have no enemies","They shall live without labor"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:28",verse:"Observe and hear all these words which I command thee, that it may go well with thee, and with thy children after thee for ever, when thou doest that which is good and right in the sight of the LORD thy God.", insight:"Well with thee and thy children for ever; obedience is the longest inheritance."},
{q:"What will God do to the nations before Israel?", options:["Cut them off from before Israel","Make them pay yearly tribute","Send them back into Egypt","Give them new gods to serve"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:29",verse:"When the LORD thy God shall cut off the nations from before thee, whither thou goest to possess them, and thou succeedest them, and dwellest in their land;", insight:"God cuts off the nations; do not pick up the gods He has just judged."},
{q:"What snare must they avoid after the nations are cut off?", options:["Enquiring after their gods, saying, How did these nations serve their gods?","Marrying their daughters","Trading with their merchants","Learning their tongue"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:30",verse:"Take heed to thyself that thou be not snared by following them, after that they be destroyed from before thee; and that thou enquire not after their gods, saying, How did these nations serve their gods? even so will I do likewise.", insight:"'How did these nations serve their gods?' Curiosity about idolatry is the first step toward it."},
{q:"What abomination had the nations done unto their gods?", options:["They burnt their sons and their daughters in the fire","They sang false songs","They built high towers","They stole from the poor"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:31",verse:"Thou shalt not do so unto the LORD thy God: for every abomination to the LORD, which he hateth, have they done unto their gods; for even their sons and their daughters they have burnt in the fire to their gods.", insight:"Sons and daughters in the fire; idolatry always ends by devouring its own children."},
{q:"What seal does Moses put on all these commands?", options:["What thing soever I command you, observe to do it: thou shalt not add thereto, nor diminish from it","Thou shalt add new feasts","Thou shalt diminish the tithe","Thou shalt change the law when it suits thee"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 12:32",verse:"What thing soever I command you, observe to do it: thou shalt not add thereto, nor diminish from it.", insight:"Neither add nor diminish; God's word comes finished, not as a draft."}
]},
{n:13, name:"The Test of False Prophets", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 13:4",verse:"Ye shall walk after the LORD your God, and fear him, and keep his commandments, and obey his voice, and ye shall serve him, and cleave unto him."}, facts:["Did you know God calls the false prophet's test a proving of Israel, to know whether they love the LORD with all their heart and soul, even when the sign actually comes true (Deuteronomy 13:3)?","Did you know 'children of Belial' means literally sons of worthlessness, a title for those who draw whole cities after other gods (Deuteronomy 13:13)?","Did you know the enticer could be one's own brother, child, or the wife of thy bosom, and still the command stands: neither shall thine eye pity him (Deuteronomy 13:6-8)?"], questions:[
{q:"What may arise among Israel to test them?", options:["A prophet, or a dreamer of dreams, giving a sign or a wonder","A king from the land of Egypt","A famine throughout the land","A plague of locusts"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:1",verse:"If there arise among you a prophet, or a dreamer of dreams, and giveth thee a sign or a wonder,", insight:"Prophet or dreamer with a sign; not every wonder comes from God."},
{q:"What if the sign or wonder actually comes to pass?", options:["If he says, Let us go after other gods, thou shalt not hearken unto him","Thou shalt follow him at once","Thou shalt make him a ruler","Thou shalt build him an altar"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:2",verse:"And the sign or the wonder come to pass, whereof he spake unto thee, saying, Let us go after other gods, which thou hast not known, and let us serve them;", insight:"Even a true sign can carry a false god; miracles never outrank the commandments."},
{q:"Why does God allow such a test?", options:["The LORD your God proveth you, to know whether ye love the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul","To confuse the people","To honor the prophet","To bring in new laws"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:3",verse:"Thou shalt not hearken unto the words of that prophet, or that dreamer of dreams: for the LORD your God proveth you, to know whether ye love the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul.", insight:"God proves you by it; tests reveal whether love for Him outruns love for signs."},
{q:"What sixfold devotion does Moses command?", options:["Walk after the LORD, fear Him, keep His commandments, obey His voice, serve Him, and cleave unto Him","Pray, fast, give, sing, dance, and shout","Build, plant, reap, store, sell, and buy","Go, see, hear, speak, run, and hide"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:4",verse:"Ye shall walk after the LORD your God, and fear him, and keep his commandments, and obey his voice, and ye shall serve him, and cleave unto him.", insight:"Walk, fear, keep, obey, serve, cleave; loyalty to God is a whole life, not a single act."},
{q:"What shall happen to that prophet or dreamer of dreams?", options:["He shall be put to death","He shall be sent into exile","He shall pay a heavy fine","He shall be made a priest"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:5",verse:"And that prophet, or that dreamer of dreams, shall be put to death; because he hath spoken to turn you away from the LORD your God, which brought you out of the land of Egypt, and redeemed you out of the house of bondage, to thrust thee out of the way which the LORD thy God commanded thee to walk in. So shalt thou put the evil away from the midst of thee.", insight:"Put to death; God treats soul murder as seriously as murder of the body."},
{q:"Why must that prophet die?", options:["Because he hath spoken to turn you away from the LORD your God, which brought you out of Egypt","Because he told a common lie","Because he was poor","Because he was a stranger"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:5",verse:"And that prophet, or that dreamer of dreams, shall be put to death; because he hath spoken to turn you away from the LORD your God, which brought you out of the land of Egypt, and redeemed you out of the house of bondage, to thrust thee out of the way which the LORD thy God commanded thee to walk in. So shalt thou put the evil away from the midst of thee.", insight:"He spoke to turn you away; leading souls from God is the gravest treason."},
{q:"Who might entice thee secretly?", options:["Thy brother, thy son, thy daughter, the wife of thy bosom, or thy friend","Only a stranger from afar","Only a priest of the tabernacle","Only a king of the nations"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:6",verse:"If thy brother, the son of thy mother, or thy son, or thy daughter, or the wife of thy bosom, or thy friend, which is as thine own soul, entice thee secretly, saying, Let us go and serve other gods, which thou hast not known, thou, nor thy fathers;", insight:"Brother, child, wife, friend; the dearest voice can carry the deadliest whisper."},
{q:"How far off might these strange gods be?", options:["Nigh unto thee, or far off, from one end of the earth even unto the other","Only across the river","Only in the land of Egypt","Only in the high mountains"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:7",verse:"Namely, of the gods of the people which are round about you, nigh unto thee, or far off from thee, from the one end of the earth even unto the other end of the earth;", insight:"From one end of the earth to the other; distance does not make a false god less false."},
{q:"What must thou not do toward the enticer?", options:["Thou shalt not consent, nor hearken; neither shall thine eye pity him, neither shalt thou spare, neither shalt thou conceal him","Thou shalt argue with him kindly","Thou shalt pay him to be silent","Thou shalt follow him in secret"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:8",verse:"Thou shalt not consent unto him, nor hearken unto him; neither shall thine eye pity him, neither shalt thou spare, neither shalt thou conceal him:", insight:"No pity, no sparing, no concealing; misplaced mercy toward evil is cruelty to the soul."},
{q:"Whose hand must be first upon the enticer?", options:["Thine own hand, and afterwards the hand of all the people","The priest's hand","The king's hand","The stranger's hand"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:9",verse:"But thou shalt surely kill him; thine hand shall be first upon him to put him to death, and afterwards the hand of all the people.", insight:"Thine hand first; responsibility for truth begins with the one who heard the lie."},
{q:"How shall the enticer die?", options:["Thou shalt stone him with stones, that he die","He shall be hanged on a tree","He shall be burned with fire","He shall be drowned in the river"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:10",verse:"And thou shalt stone him with stones, that he die; because he hath sought to thrust thee away from the LORD thy God, which brought thee out of the land of Egypt, from the house of bondage.", insight:"Stoned with stones; the whole congregation bore witness that God alone is God."},
{q:"What will all Israel do when they hear of it?", options:["All Israel shall hear, and fear, and shall do no more any such wickedness","All Israel shall mourn for him","All Israel shall flee the land","All Israel shall rejoice greatly"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:11",verse:"And all Israel shall hear, and fear, and shall do no more any such wickedness as this is among you.", insight:"Hear and fear; righteous judgment teaches the whole nation what words cannot."},
{q:"In what places might this evil be heard of?", options:["In one of thy cities, which the LORD thy God hath given thee to dwell there","In the land of Egypt","In the midst of the sea","In the wilderness of Sinai"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:12",verse:"If thou shalt hear say in one of thy cities, which the LORD thy God hath given thee to dwell there, saying,", insight:"In one of thy cities; corruption can take root in the very towns God gave you."},
{q:"Who are the 'children of Belial'?", options:["Certain men gone out from among you, who withdraw the inhabitants of their city after other gods","The sons of the priests","The children of the king","Foreign merchants from afar"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:13",verse:"Certain men, the children of Belial, are gone out from among you, and have withdrawn the inhabitants of their city, saying, Let us go and serve other gods, which ye have not known;", insight:"Children of Belial, sons of worthlessness; evil rarely works alone, it recruits."},
{q:"What must be done before judging the city?", options:["Thou shalt enquire, and make search, and ask diligently","Thou shalt attack it at once","Thou shalt wait forty days","Thou shalt send a spy by night"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:14",verse:"Then shalt thou enquire, and make search, and ask diligently; and, behold, if it be truth, and the thing certain, that such abomination is wrought among you;", insight:"Enquire, search, ask diligently; even in judgment, God commands careful truth."},
{q:"What if the report about the city is true?", options:["Thou shalt surely smite the inhabitants of that city with the edge of the sword, destroying it utterly, and all therein, and the cattle","Thou shalt forgive them all","Thou shalt lay a tax upon them","Thou shalt drive them into exile"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:15",verse:"Thou shalt surely smite the inhabitants of that city with the edge of the sword, destroying it utterly, and all that is therein, and the cattle thereof, with the edge of the sword.", insight:"Destroying it utterly; a city given wholly to idols forfeits its place."},
{q:"What is to be done with the spoil of that city?", options:["Gather it into the midst of the street, and burn the city and all the spoil with fire, for the LORD","Divide it among the soldiers","Keep it in the treasury","Give it unto the poor"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:16",verse:"And thou shalt gather all the spoil of it into the midst of the street thereof, and shalt burn with fire the city, and all the spoil thereof every whit, for the LORD thy God: and it shall be an heap for ever; it shall not be built again.", insight:"Burned every whit for the LORD; nothing of idolatry is worth keeping."},
{q:"What shall that city become?", options:["An heap for ever; it shall not be built again","A memorial park for travelers","A new capital city","A busy market town"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:16",verse:"And thou shalt gather all the spoil of it into the midst of the street thereof, and shalt burn with fire the city, and all the spoil thereof every whit, for the LORD thy God: and it shall be an heap for ever; it shall not be built again.", insight:"An heap for ever, never rebuilt; some ruins must preach forever."},
{q:"What must not cleave to thine hand?", options:["Nought of the cursed thing","The gold of the city","The cattle of the field","The garments of the slain"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:17",verse:"And there shall cleave nought of the cursed thing to thine hand: that the LORD may turn from the fierceness of his anger, and shew thee mercy, and have compassion upon thee, and multiply thee, as he hath sworn unto thy fathers;", insight:"Nought of the cursed thing; take nothing from judgment, lest judgment take you."},
{q:"What follows when Israel hearkens to the LORD's voice?", options:["The LORD will turn from the fierceness of His anger, and shew thee mercy, and multiply thee","The land will dry up and fail","The enemies will return again","The cities will fall into ruin"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 13:17",verse:"And there shall cleave nought of the cursed thing to thine hand: that the LORD may turn from the fierceness of his anger, and shew thee mercy, and have compassion upon thee, and multiply thee, as he hath sworn unto thy fathers;", insight:"Mercy and multiplying; turning from idols turns God's anger into blessing."}
]},
{n:14, name:"Clean and Unclean", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 14:2",verse:"for thou art an holy people unto the LORD thy God, and the LORD hath chosen thee to be a peculiar people unto himself, above all the nations that are upon the earth."}, facts:["Did you know 'thou shalt not seethe a kid in his mother's milk' was aimed at a Canaanite fertility rite, and Jewish tradition later built the whole separation of meat and dairy on this one line (Deuteronomy 14:21)?","Did you know the food laws use two signs for clean land animals: parting the hoof and chewing the cud, and an animal needs both to pass (Deuteronomy 14:6)?","Did you know the third year tithe was a welfare tithe: stored within thy gates so the Levite, the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow could eat and be satisfied (Deuteronomy 14:28-29)?"], questions:[
{q:"What are the children of the LORD forbidden to do for the dead?", options:["Cut themselves, nor make any baldness between their eyes","Weep at all","Fast for seven days","Wear sackcloth in the gate"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:1",verse:"Ye are the children of the LORD your God: ye shall not cut yourselves, nor make any baldness between your eyes for the dead.", insight:"No cuttings, no baldness; God's children do not borrow the mourning rites of idols."},
{q:"What is Israel unto the LORD?", options:["An holy people, chosen to be a peculiar people unto Himself, above all the nations","A common nation like the rest","A forgotten people","A people without a law"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:2",verse:"for thou art an holy people unto the LORD thy God, and the LORD hath chosen thee to be a peculiar people unto himself, above all the nations that are upon the earth.", insight:"A peculiar people; holiness means belonging to God in a way the world is not."},
{q:"What are the two signs of a clean beast?", options:["It parteth the hoof and cleaveth the cleft, and cheweth the cud","It has horns and a long tail","It is large and strong","It lives in the open field"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:6",verse:"And every beast that parteth the hoof, and cleaveth the cleft into two claws, and cheweth the cud among the beasts, that ye shall eat.", insight:"Hoof and cud together; outward walk and inward chewing must both be clean."},
{q:"Which animals chew the cud but are unclean?", options:["The camel, the hare, and the coney, because they divide not the hoof","The ox and the sheep","The goat and the deer","The horse and the donkey"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:7",verse:"Nevertheless these ye shall not eat of them that chew the cud, or of them that divide the cloven hoof; as the camel, and the hare, and the coney: for they chew the cud, but divide not the hoof; therefore they are unclean unto you.", insight:"Camel, hare, and coney; half the signs is not enough, God requires both."},
{q:"Why is the swine unclean?", options:["It divideth the hoof, yet cheweth not the cud","It is too small to eat","It lives in the mud","It has no horns"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:8",verse:"And the swine, because it divideth the hoof, yet cheweth not the cud, it is unclean unto you: ye shall not eat of their flesh, nor touch their dead carcase.", insight:"The swine divides the hoof but chews not the cud; appearances of cleanness deceive."},
{q:"What water creatures may be eaten?", options:["Whatsoever hath fins and scales","Only the great fish of the sea","Whatsoever swims the fastest","Only the fish of the rivers"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:9",verse:"These ye shall eat of all that are in the waters: all that have fins and scales shall ye eat:", insight:"Fins and scales; God marks the clean with signs you can see."},
{q:"What water creatures may not be eaten?", options:["Whatsoever hath not fins and scales","Whatsoever is too small","Whatsoever lives in the deep","Whatsoever has spots"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:10",verse:"And whatsoever hath not fins and scales ye may not eat; it is unclean unto you.", insight:"No fins, no scales, no table; God draws lines and calls them holy."},
{q:"Which birds are named as unclean?", options:["The eagle, the ossifrage, and the ospray","The dove and the sparrow","The swallow and the crane","The cock and the hen"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:12",verse:"But these are they of which ye shall not eat: the eagle, and ossifrage, and the ospray,", insight:"Eagle, ossifrage, ospray; birds of prey are kept off the table of a holy people."},
{q:"Which bird after his kind is unclean?", options:["Every raven after his kind","Every dove","Every sparrow","Every quail"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:14",verse:"And every raven after his kind,", insight:"Every raven after his kind; God names the unclean one by one, so none is missed."},
{q:"Which of these are unclean birds?", options:["The little owl, and the great owl, and the swan","The turtledove","The young pigeon","The sparrow of the field"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:16",verse:"The little owl, and the great owl, and the swan,", insight:"Little owl, great owl, swan; holiness reaches even to the birds of the field."},
{q:"Which winged creature in the list is not a bird?", options:["The bat","The stork","The heron","The lapwing"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:18",verse:"And the stork, and the heron after her kind, and the lapwing, and the bat.", insight:"The bat flies but is unclean; not everything with wings belongs on the wing of faith."},
{q:"What does Moses say of every creeping thing that flieth?", options:["It is unclean unto you; ye shall not eat of them","It is clean for food","It may be eaten on feast days","It belongs to the priests alone"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:19",verse:"And every creeping thing that flieth is unclean unto you: they shall not be eaten.", insight:"Every creeping thing that flieth is unclean; God leaves no loophole for the swarm."},
{q:"What may they do with anything that dieth of itself?", options:["Give it unto the stranger, or sell it unto an alien, but not eat of it","Bury it outside the camp","Burn it with fire","Offer it as a sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:21",verse:"Ye shall not eat of any thing that dieth of itself: thou shalt give it unto the stranger that is in thy gates, that he may eat it; or thou mayest sell it unto an alien: for thou art an holy people unto the LORD thy God. Thou shalt not seethe a kid in his mother’s milk.", insight:"Not eaten by the holy, yet not wasted; God orders even what we refuse."},
{q:"What cooking practice is forbidden?", options:["Thou shalt not seethe a kid in his mother's milk","Thou shalt not roast the lamb","Thou shalt not bake the bread","Thou shalt not boil the herbs"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:21",verse:"Ye shall not eat of any thing that dieth of itself: thou shalt give it unto the stranger that is in thy gates, that he may eat it; or thou mayest sell it unto an alien: for thou art an holy people unto the LORD thy God. Thou shalt not seethe a kid in his mother’s milk.", insight:"Not a kid in his mother's milk; God will not have mercy turned into cruelty."},
{q:"What must they tithe?", options:["All the increase of their seed, that the field bringeth forth year by year","Only the firstfruits","Only the cattle of the field","Only the gold and silver"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:22",verse:"Thou shalt truly tithe all the increase of thy seed, that the field bringeth forth year by year.", insight:"All the increase, year by year; the tithe is a habit, not an occasion."},
{q:"Why eat the tithe before the LORD?", options:["That thou mayest learn to fear the LORD thy God always","That thou mayest become rich","That thou mayest feed the priests","That thou mayest store up food"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:23",verse:"And thou shalt eat before the LORD thy God, in the place which he shall choose to place his name there, the tithe of thy corn, of thy wine, and of thine oil, and the firstlings of thy herds and of thy flocks; that thou mayest learn to fear the LORD thy God always.", insight:"Learn to fear the LORD always; the tithe is a school, and the classroom is the table."},
{q:"What may they do if the way to God's chosen place is too long?", options:["Turn the tithe into money, and bind up the money in their hand","Keep the tithe at home","Give the tithe to the poor","Skip the tithe that year"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:25",verse:"Then shalt thou turn it into money, and bind up the money in thine hand, and shalt go unto the place which the LORD thy God shall choose:", insight:"Turn it into money and bind it in hand; God makes room for distance, not for disobedience."},
{q:"What may they buy with the tithe money?", options:["Whatsoever their soul lusteth after: oxen, sheep, wine, or strong drink; and eat and rejoice before the LORD","Only bread and water","Only sacrifices for the altar","Only garments for the feast"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:26",verse:"And thou shalt bestow that money for whatsoever thy soul lusteth after, for oxen, or for sheep, or for wine, or for strong drink, or for whatsoever thy soul desireth: and thou shalt eat there before the LORD thy God, and thou shalt rejoice, thou, and thine household,", insight:"Oxen, sheep, wine; God loves a rejoicing household, and He pays for the feast."},
{q:"When is the special tithe brought forth?", options:["At the end of three years, laid up within thy gates","Every sabbath day","Once in a lifetime","At every new moon"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:28",verse:"At the end of three years thou shalt bring forth all the tithe of thine increase the same year, and shalt lay it up within thy gates:", insight:"Every three years within thy gates; generosity gets a calendar, not just an impulse."},
{q:"Who eats of the third year tithe?", options:["The Levite, the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow, that they may eat and be satisfied","Only the priests of the altar","Only the king and his house","Only the rich of the land"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 14:29",verse:"And the Levite, (because he hath no part nor inheritance with thee,) and the stranger, and the fatherless, and the widow, which are within thy gates, shall come, and shall eat and be satisfied; that the LORD thy God may bless thee in all the work of thine hand which thou doest.", insight:"Levite, stranger, fatherless, widow; God's storehouse feeds the ones the world forgets."}
]},
{n:15, name:"The Year of Release", seal:{ref:"Deuteronomy 15:11",verse:"For the poor shall never cease out of the land: therefore I command thee, saying, Thou shalt open thine hand wide unto thy brother, to thy poor, and to thy needy, in thy land."}, facts:["Did you know the seventh year release canceled debts, not just postponed them, and it was called 'the LORD's release' (Deuteronomy 15:2)?","Did you know 'the poor shall never cease out of the land' is the line Jesus quotes at Bethany when the disciples grumble about the ointment poured on Him (Deuteronomy 15:11; Matthew 26:11)?","Did you know a servant who chose to stay was marked by having his ear bored through with an awl against the doorpost, a lifelong sign of chosen service (Deuteronomy 15:17)?"], questions:[
{q:"When is the release to be made?", options:["At the end of every seven years","Every month","Every sabbath day","Once in a lifetime"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:1",verse:"At the end of every seven years thou shalt make a release.", insight:"Every seven years; God builds rest into the economy, not just into the week."},
{q:"What is the LORD's release?", options:["Every creditor shall release what he lent his neighbour, and not exact it of him","Every debtor shall pay double","Every loan shall be renewed for seven more years","Every creditor shall seize the pledge"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:2",verse:"And this is the manner of the release: Every creditor that lendeth ought unto his neighbour shall release it; he shall not exact it of his neighbour, or of his brother; because it is called the LORD’S release.", insight:"'It is called the LORD's release'; debts die by divine decree, not by payment."},
{q:"Of whom may the creditor still exact the debt?", options:["Of a foreigner","Of his brother","Of the widow","Of the Levite"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:3",verse:"Of a foreigner thou mayest exact it again: but that which is thine with thy brother thine hand shall release;", insight:"Of a foreigner thou mayest exact it; the covenant's mercy starts at home."},
{q:"What does Moses say shall be among them?", options:["Save when there shall be no poor among you","There shall be no rich men","There shall be no work to do","There shall be no strangers"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:4",verse:"Save when there shall be no poor among you; for the LORD shall greatly bless thee in the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee for an inheritance to possess it:", insight:"'No poor among you'; God's blessing aims at an economy with no one left behind."},
{q:"What will obedience make Israel?", options:["They shall lend unto many nations, but shall not borrow","They shall borrow from many nations","They shall rule by the sword","They shall have no trade at all"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:6",verse:"For the LORD thy God blesseth thee, as he promised thee: and thou shalt lend unto many nations, but thou shalt not borrow; and thou shalt reign over many nations, but they shall not reign over thee.", insight:"Lend and not borrow; obedience turns a nation of former slaves into lenders."},
{q:"What must they not do toward a poor brother?", options:["Harden their heart, nor shut their hand from him","Lend to him in secret","Teach him a trade first","Send him away empty"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:7",verse:"If there be among you a poor man of one of thy brethren within any of thy gates in thy land which the LORD thy God giveth thee, thou shalt not harden thine heart, nor shut thine hand from thy poor brother:", insight:"Nor harden, nor shut; the hand and the heart open together, or not at all."},
{q:"What must they do instead?", options:["Open their hand wide unto him, and surely lend him sufficient for his need","Give him only good advice","Lend him half of what he asks","Wait seven years to help him"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:8",verse:"But thou shalt open thine hand wide unto him, and shalt surely lend him sufficient for his need, in that which he wanteth.", insight:"Open wide, sufficient for his need; generosity is measured by the need, not by the surplus."},
{q:"What wicked thought must they beware of?", options:["The seventh year is at hand, so I will give my poor brother nought","The poor are lazy and deserve it","The release is too hard to keep","The law is too old to follow"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:9",verse:"Beware that there be not a thought in thy wicked heart, saying, The seventh year, the year of release, is at hand; and thine eye be evil against thy poor brother, and thou givest him nought; and he cry unto the LORD against thee, and it be sin unto thee.", insight:"Beware the calendar of greed; counting down to release is counting up your own loss."},
{q:"How should they give?", options:["Surely give him, and the heart shall not be grieved when thou givest","Give with a heavy and grieving heart","Give only in secret places","Give only once a year"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:10",verse:"Thou shalt surely give him, and thine heart shall not be grieved when thou givest unto him: because that for this thing the LORD thy God shall bless thee in all thy works, and in all that thou puttest thine hand unto.", insight:"Give, and grieve not; a cheerless gift loses the blessing it was meant to carry."},
{q:"Why does Moses command open handedness?", options:["For the poor shall never cease out of the land","For the rich will soon leave","For the harvest will surely fail","For the law will soon end"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:11",verse:"For the poor shall never cease out of the land: therefore I command thee, saying, Thou shalt open thine hand wide unto thy brother, to thy poor, and to thy needy, in thy land.", insight:"The poor never cease; neither, then, should the open hand."},
{q:"How long shall the Hebrew servant serve?", options:["Six years, and in the seventh he shall go out free from thee","Three years and no more","Twelve years of labor","For the rest of his life"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:12",verse:"And if thy brother, an Hebrew man, or an Hebrew woman, be sold unto thee, and serve thee six years; then in the seventh year thou shalt let him go free from thee.", insight:"Six years, then free; no bondage in Israel is meant to be forever."},
{q:"How must the freed servant be sent away?", options:["Not empty","With chains upon him","In secret by night","At midnight"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:13",verse:"And when thou sendest him out free from thee, thou shalt not let him go away empty:", insight:"Not empty; freedom with nothing is only a longer chain."},
{q:"Out of what shall they furnish him liberally?", options:["Out of thy flock, and out of thy floor, and out of thy winepress","Out of the king's treasury","Out of the temple storehouse","Out of the spoil of war"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:14",verse:"Thou shalt furnish him liberally out of thy flock, and out of thy floor, and out of thy winepress: of that wherewith the LORD thy God hath blessed thee thou shalt give unto him.", insight:"Flock, floor, winepress; share from what God used to bless you, in the same kinds."},
{q:"What must they remember?", options:["That thou wast a bondman in the land of Egypt, and the LORD thy God redeemed thee","That Egypt was kind to them","That Pharaoh was a wise king","That the wilderness was easy"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:15",verse:"And thou shalt remember that thou wast a bondman in the land of Egypt, and the LORD thy God redeemed thee: therefore I command thee this thing to day.", insight:"Remember thou wast a bondman; memory of mercy is the engine of mercy."},
{q:"What if the servant loves his master and will not go away?", options:["He may stay, if he says, I will not go away from thee","He must still be sent away","He must pay for his freedom","He must serve ten more years"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:16",verse:"And it shall be, if he say unto thee, I will not go away from thee; because he loveth thee and thine house, because he is well with thee;", insight:"Love can choose the house; some bonds are forged by affection, not by chains."},
{q:"What marks the servant who stays for ever?", options:["His master takes an aul, and thrusts it through his ear unto the door","He is branded upon the forehead","He wears a ring of iron","He is given a new name"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:17",verse:"Then thou shalt take an aul, and thrust it through his ear unto the door, and he shall be thy servant for ever. And also unto thy maidservant thou shalt do likewise.", insight:"The awl through the ear at the door; chosen service leaves a lifelong mark."},
{q:"Why should freeing the servant not seem hard?", options:["For he hath been worth a double hired servant to thee, in serving thee six years","For he was lazy and slow","For he was old and weak","For he was sickly"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:18",verse:"It shall not seem hard unto thee, when thou sendest him away free from thee; for he hath been worth a double hired servant to thee, in serving thee six years: and the LORD thy God shall bless thee in all that thou doest.", insight:"Worth a double hired servant; six years of faithful work has already paid you twice."},
{q:"What is to be done with the firstling males?", options:["Sanctify them unto the LORD; do no work with the firstling of the bullock, nor shear the firstling of the sheep","Sell them in the market","Eat them at home","Give them unto the poor"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:19",verse:"All the firstling males that come of thy herd and of thy flock thou shalt sanctify unto the LORD thy God: thou shalt do no work with the firstling of thy bullock, nor shear the firstling of thy sheep.", insight:"Sanctified, not shorn nor worked; the first belongs to God untouched."},
{q:"What firstling may not be sacrificed?", options:["If there be any blemish therein, as if it be lame, or blind","The largest of the flock","The firstborn of twins","The male of the herd"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:21",verse:"And if there be any blemish therein, as if it be lame, or blind, or have any ill blemish, thou shalt not sacrifice it unto the LORD thy God.", insight:"Lame or blind, not sacrificed; God deserves the unblemished, not the leftover."},
{q:"What must not be eaten of the firstling?", options:["The blood; thou shalt pour it upon the ground as water","The fat of the kidneys","The flesh of the shoulder","The bones of the legs"], a:0, ref:"Deuteronomy 15:23",verse:"Only thou shalt not eat the blood thereof; thou shalt pour it upon the ground as water.", insight:"Blood poured as water; even in feasting, the life returns to the ground and to God."}
]}
]);
